DAY_DATA = {'day': 155, 'part1_intro': "Day 155 — Altostrat Media — architecture defense — uses the roadmap's case or exam scope as the input. Each topic names the decision boundary, evidence owner and business effect; no product choice or score is treated as a fact without supporting evidence.", 'part2_intro': 'Trace the full reasoning path: supplied fact or requirement, candidate design or study rule, acceptance evidence, failure signal, owner and condition that would change the choice. The topology is a teaching model, not evidence of a live system or exam result.', 'part3_intro': 'These deep-dive cases preserve the original case or exam reasoning while separating supplied facts from architectural inference. The incident diagrams are synthetic exercises, not observed production events.', 'part4_intro': "The labs retain each day's original decision work, expanded into the eight execution stages used on Day 142. Complete them with prior artifacts and synthetic inputs unless an earlier roadmap page explicitly authorizes a cloud test.", 'exit_summary': 'An ADR covering quality, auditability, hybrid operations and cost with one rejected option.', 'arch_table_html': '\n<table><caption>Day-specific architecture and evidence path</caption><thead><tr><th>Topic boundary</th><th>Decision rule</th><th>Acceptance evidence</th><th>Limit</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>Compare designs for AI-assisted discovery and support</td><td>Separate supplied fact, requirement and proposed control.</td><td>One artifact, one rejected alternative and one changed-constraint result.</td><td>Local/tabletop evidence cannot prove production behavior or exam performance.</td></tr><tr><td>Auditability, hybrid operations, CI/CD and cost are part of the AI design</td><td>Separate supplied fact, requirement and proposed control.</td><td>One artifact, one rejected alternative and one changed-constraint result.</td><td>Local/tabletop evidence cannot prove production behavior or exam performance.</td></tr></tbody></table>', 'arch_diagram': {'type': 'topology', 'title': 'Day 155: Altostrat Media — architecture defense — evidence and decision path', 'desc': 'Three-tier architecture path for Altostrat Media — architecture defense, showing case or exam inputs, requirements and trade-off evidence, then acceptance and ownership controls.', 'caption': 'Scope: a synthetic evidence path for Day 155 covering Compare designs for AI-assisted discovery  / Auditability, hybrid operations, CI/CD and. It shows reasoning boundaries and verification ownership; it does not prove a production deployment, exam result, price, quota, eligibility or customer outcome.', 'width': 1120, 'height': 690, 'layers': [{'name': 'TIER 1 · INPUTS / DEMAND', 'desc': 'case facts, prompts and constraints', 'x': 10, 'y': 55, 'w': 1100, 'h': 92, 'fill': '#0c2033', 'title_color': '#38bdf8', 'opacity': 0.72}, {'name': 'TIER 2 · EVIDENCE / REASONING', 'desc': 'requirements, alternatives and failure checks', 'x': 10, 'y': 185, 'w': 1100, 'h': 210, 'fill': '#241808', 'title_color': '#f59e0b', 'opacity': 0.64}, {'name': 'TIER 3 · GOVERNANCE / ACCEPTANCE', 'desc': 'owners, acceptance and revisit triggers', 'x': 10, 'y': 435, 'w': 1100, 'h': 115, 'fill': '#062316', 'title_color': '#22c55e', 'opacity': 0.68}], 'components': [{'name': 'Case or prompt', 'detail': 'Day 155 supplied scope', 'x': 60, 'y': 78, 'w': 250, 'h': 56, 'stroke': '#38bdf8', 'fill': '#102a42'}, {'name': 'Prior artifacts', 'detail': 'facts + decisions + errors', 'x': 435, 'y': 78, 'w': 250, 'h': 56, 'stroke': '#38bdf8', 'fill': '#102a42'}, {'name': 'Changed constraint', 'detail': 'cost / risk / scope', 'x': 810, 'y': 78, 'w': 250, 'h': 56, 'stroke': '#38bdf8', 'fill': '#102a42'}, {'name': 'Requirements map', 'detail': 'fact to acceptance', 'x': 60, 'y': 220, 'w': 250, 'h': 105, 'stroke': '#f59e0b', 'fill': '#3b2508'}, {'name': 'Option matrix', 'detail': 'choice + alternative', 'x': 435, 'y': 220, 'w': 250, 'h': 105, 'stroke': '#f59e0b', 'fill': '#3b2508'}, {'name': 'Failure rehearsal', 'detail': 'signal + safe response', 'x': 810, 'y': 220, 'w': 250, 'h': 105, 'stroke': '#f59e0b', 'fill': '#3b2508'}, {'name': 'Evidence owner', 'detail': 'source + artifact', 'x': 245, 'y': 455, 'w': 250, 'h': 70, 'stroke': '#22c55e', 'fill': '#064e3b'}, {'name': 'Acceptance gate', 'detail': 'observed / predicted', 'x': 625, 'y': 455, 'w': 250, 'h': 70, 'stroke': '#22c55e', 'fill': '#064e3b'}], 'flows': [{'x1': 185, 'y1': 134, 'x2': 185, 'y2': 220, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'extract'}, {'x1': 560, 'y1': 134, 'x2': 560, 'y2': 220, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'trace'}, {'x1': 935, 'y1': 134, 'x2': 935, 'y2': 220, 'type': 'warn', 'label': 'challenge'}, {'x1': 310, 'y1': 272, 'x2': 435, 'y2': 272, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'compare'}, {'x1': 685, 'y1': 272, 'x2': 810, 'y2': 272, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'rehearse'}, {'x1': 935, 'y1': 325, 'x2': 750, 'y2': 455, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'accept'}, {'x1': 560, 'y1': 325, 'x2': 370, 'y2': 455, 'type': 'warn', 'label': 'evidence'}, {'x1': 495, 'y1': 490, 'x2': 625, 'y2': 490, 'type': 'ok', 'label': 'review'}], 'boundaries': [{'x': 42, 'y': 205, 'w': 1036, 'h': 140, 'color': '#f59e0b', 'label': 'EVIDENCE CHECK'}, {'x': 220, 'y': 442, 'w': 680, 'h': 94, 'color': '#22c55e', 'label': 'DECISION OWNER'}], 'probes': [{'cx': 185, 'cy': 106, 'label': 'PROBE 1 · input classified', 'badge': 'P1', 'color': '#38bdf8'}, {'cx': 560, 'cy': 272, 'label': 'PROBE 2 · trade-off recorded', 'badge': 'P2', 'color': '#f59e0b'}, {'cx': 750, 'cy': 490, 'label': 'PROBE 3 · acceptance result', 'badge': 'P3', 'color': '#22c55e'}]}, 'topics': [{'key': 'topic-01', 'title': 'Compare designs for AI-assisted discovery and support', 'overview': 'Defend an AI-assisted media design using the Day 154 requirements matrix. Compare a grounded retrieval path with a more tightly controlled workflow, and make the choice depend on latency, quality, auditability, hybrid access and operator capability.', 'preview': 'Symptom: Altostrat connects a conversational assistant directly to a broad content store. Effect: The compare designs for ai-assisted discovery and support decision remains unverified.', 'technical': '<p>Separate the user request path from the content-processing path. A discovery request may retrieve approved metadata and excerpts, assemble a grounded response and return a safe fallback. A summarization or enrichment job can be queued, retried, evaluated and reviewed before publication. The two paths have different latency, retry, cost and failure requirements.</p><table><caption>Altostrat architecture-defense matrix</caption><thead><tr><th>Boundary</th><th>Option A</th><th>Option B</th><th>Decision evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Retrieval</td><td>Curated index of approved metadata and transcript excerpts</td><td>Direct warehouse or object queries behind a controlled service</td><td>Freshness, access policy, corpus size and measured response path</td></tr><tr><td>AI orchestration</td><td>Managed model endpoint with bounded tools</td><td>Containerized orchestration with explicit model/version controls</td><td>Model availability, skills, audit requirements and rollback mechanism</td></tr><tr><td>Hybrid operation</td><td>Cloud-first path with a private integration boundary</td><td>Portable service contract that can run across cloud and on-premises</td><td>Data locality, connectivity failure behavior and deployment ownership</td></tr><tr><td>Delivery</td><td>Centralized CI/CD with signed artifacts and staged rollout</td><td>Team-owned pipelines with shared policy checks</td><td>Change lead time, evidence quality, separation of duties and toil</td></tr></tbody></table><p>CDN and transcoding can support the case, but they do not solve AI grounding, auditability or review. State the control that prevents a model from retrieving restricted material, taking an unauthorized action or publishing an unreviewed result. Include a model/configuration identifier and a rollback target in every decision record.</p><p><a href="../sources.html#topic-047">Topic 047 source section</a>; current publisher material was checked 2026-09-30. Separate supplied facts, local observations and proposed controls.</p>', 'questions': ['Which requirement bounds the selected option?', 'What observable evidence supports the decision?', 'Which changed constraint would reverse the choice?', 'Who owns the failure response and review?'], 'reference': 'https://services.google.com/fh/files/misc/v6.1_pca_altostrat_media_case_study_english.pdf', 'reference_label': 'Official Topic 47 source (checked 2026-09-30)', 'scenario': {'scenario': 'Altostrat connects a conversational assistant directly to a broad content store. The demo is fast, but the team cannot show which source version supported a response, whether a user was authorized to see it, or how to revert a bad prompt/model change. A stale or restricted asset can become an answer or recommendation.', 'impact': '', 'constraints': 'Use synthetic data, preserve the prior artifact and keep unknown behavior explicitly labeled.', 'facts': 'The case statement and artifact are teaching inputs; no production incident or learner result is claimed.', 'inference': 'The design optimized the response path before defining corpus boundaries and evidence. Split approved retrieval from source storage, bind each answer to source/version metadata, use bounded tools and add refusal/degraded behavior. Stage model and prompt changes against an evaluation set, then canary and roll back by version.', 'root': 'The design optimized the response path before defining corpus boundaries and evidence. Split approved retrieval from source storage, bind each answer to source/version metadata, use bounded tools and add refusal/degraded behavior. Stage model and prompt changes against an evaluation set, then canary and roll back by version.', 'fix': 'The design optimized the response path before defining corpus boundaries and evidence. Split approved retrieval from source storage, bind each answer to source/version metadata, use bounded tools and add refusal/degraded behavior. Stage model and prompt changes against an evaluation set, then canary and roll back by version.', 'verify': 'Re-run the bounded case, compare it with the declared acceptance signal and save the resulting decision trace.', 'residual': 'A tabletop can expose control gaps but cannot prove model quality across all media, languages or users. Track the unresolved evaluation and data-owner decisions.', 'diagram': ('supplied trigger', 'missing or untested control', 'business and operating impact', 'bounded defensive control', 'verified evidence artifact')}, 'lab': {'name': 'Defend two content and AI integration options', 'goal': 'Produce an ADR comparing two feasible AI integration options and rehearse one failure in the selected path.', 'expected': 'An ADR with a selected option, rejected alternative, measurable acceptance signals, rollback path and open questions.', 'mode': 'local/tabletop with synthetic data; no cloud access or spend', 'prereq': 'Bring the prior case or exam artifact and record it unavailable if missing.', 'preflight': 'Use `day-155-01-defend-two-content-and-ai-integratio.md`; record the source, access date, prior artifact, owner and synthetic-data boundary.', 'steps': ['**Stage 1 — Preflight and validate assumptions/environment.** Create `day-155-01-defend-two-content-and-ai-integratio.md`. Record Day 155, the prior artifact, the source `https://services.google.com/fh/files/misc/v6.1_pca_altostrat_media_case_study_english.pdf`, the access date, a named owner and the statement that the exercise uses synthetic or tabletop evidence only.', '**Stage 2 — Prepare the target, inputs, or backing resources.** Freeze the inputs. Create day-155-altostrat-defense.md ; copy the Day 154 requirements and mark facts, inferences and questions.', '**Stage 3 — Author the plan, configuration, or analysis.** Draft options. For each option record retrieval boundary, model path, identity, hybrid dependency, CI/CD, storage cost, observability and rollback.', '**Stage 4 — Execute or simulate the planned change.** Set acceptance. Define quality, grounding, audit, latency, cost and safe-failure signals. Do not invent target values; write missing targets as questions.', '**Stage 5 — Inspect expected state and verify outcomes.** Change a constraint. Make hybrid connectivity unavailable, model quality insufficient or the review queue saturated. Record the first affected boundary and the alternative response.', '**Stage 6 — Rehearse a bounded failure, edge case, or decision challenge.** Defend. Write the choice, rejected option, revisit trigger, owner and residual risk. Link every material claim to the case or a dated test.', '**Stage 7 — Diagnose evidence and record remediation/decision.** Close out. Save the ADR and update the Day 155 artifact index.', '**Stage 8 — Clean up or close out the exercise.** Save `day-155-01-defend-two-content-and-ai-integratio.md`, link it from the daily artifact, keep the evidence, remove only disposable copies and state what needs an authorized or production verification.'], 'verification': 'An ADR with a selected option, rejected alternative, measurable acceptance signals, rollback path and open questions.', 'accept': 'The saved artifact identifies the requirement, selected and rejected options, acceptance evidence, failure response, owner and residual risk.', 'trouble': 'If one option wins only because it names more managed services, return to the requirement and evidence columns; managed does not mean risk-free.', 'cleanup': 'Keep the evidence artifact and remove only disposable copies. No cloud resource, credential, payment detail or protected exam content belongs in this exercise.', 'file': 'day-155-01-defend-two-content-and-ai-integratio.md'}}, {'key': 'topic-02', 'title': 'Auditability, hybrid operations, CI/CD and cost are part of the AI design', 'overview': 'The architecture is acceptable only when the operating model is acceptable. Include release provenance, identity ownership, cost attribution, storage lifecycle, hybrid incident response and the people who review or reverse AI decisions.', 'preview': 'Symptom: A new model and index refresh are deployed successfully, but response cost and review backlog rise. Effect: The auditability, hybrid operations, ci/cd and cost are part of the ai design decision remains unverified.', 'technical': '<p>Use a chain of custody for AI changes: source asset or event, transformation, model and prompt/configuration version, output, reviewer or policy decision, publication state and retention. CI/CD should test infrastructure and application changes, scan artifacts, enforce policy and make staged rollback possible. Observability should connect user experience, queue age, model error, data freshness, spend and human-review backlog.</p><p>Cost is a design variable, not a final spreadsheet. Compare hot versus colder media storage, repeated model inference, egress, index refresh, GPU/CPU use, and human review. A low unit price can be defeated by retries, duplicate processing or an over-broad corpus. For hybrid operations, name the on-premises owner, private path, degraded behavior and evidence needed when the link fails.</p><div class="callout"><strong>Defense rule</strong><p>Reject any architecture sentence of the form “AI makes it automatic” unless it names the input, authorization boundary, evaluation, output owner, audit record and safe response to uncertainty.</p></div><p><a href="../sources.html#topic-047">Topic 047 source section</a>; current publisher material was checked 2026-09-30. Separate supplied facts, local observations and proposed controls.</p>', 'questions': ['Which requirement bounds the selected option?', 'What observable evidence supports the decision?', 'Which changed constraint would reverse the choice?', 'Who owns the failure response and review?'], 'reference': 'https://services.google.com/fh/files/misc/v6.1_pca_altostrat_media_case_study_english.pdf', 'reference_label': 'Official Topic 47 source (checked 2026-09-30)', 'scenario': {'scenario': 'A new model and index refresh are deployed successfully, but response cost and review backlog rise. The pipeline records deployment success without linking the release to model quality, queue age or spend. Hybrid workers run a different configuration than cloud workers.', 'impact': '', 'constraints': 'Use synthetic data, preserve the prior artifact and keep unknown behavior explicitly labeled.', 'facts': 'The case statement and artifact are teaching inputs; no production incident or learner result is claimed.', 'inference': 'The release measure was too narrow. Add versioned configuration, environment parity checks, cost and quality gates, queue/backlog alerts, and a canary with rollback. Assign one owner to reconcile cloud and on-premises versions and another to approve content-policy changes.', 'root': 'The release measure was too narrow. Add versioned configuration, environment parity checks, cost and quality gates, queue/backlog alerts, and a canary with rollback. Assign one owner to reconcile cloud and on-premises versions and another to approve content-policy changes.', 'fix': 'The release measure was too narrow. Add versioned configuration, environment parity checks, cost and quality gates, queue/backlog alerts, and a canary with rollback. Assign one owner to reconcile cloud and on-premises versions and another to approve content-policy changes.', 'verify': 'Re-run the bounded case, compare it with the declared acceptance signal and save the resulting decision trace.', 'residual': 'Alerts are evidence, not automatic remediation. Keep a bounded shutdown or traffic-reduction playbook and verify it with synthetic content.', 'diagram': ('supplied trigger', 'missing or untested control', 'business and operating impact', 'bounded defensive control', 'verified evidence artifact')}, 'lab': {'name': 'Build the operating-evidence row for the chosen design', 'goal': 'Connect release, runtime, quality, cost and incident signals to the AI architecture.', 'expected': 'A traceable operating matrix that makes AI quality, cost, release and hybrid drift observable.', 'mode': 'local/tabletop with synthetic data; no cloud access or spend', 'prereq': 'Bring the prior case or exam artifact and record it unavailable if missing.', 'preflight': 'Use `day-155-02-build-the-operating-evidence-row-for.md`; record the source, access date, prior artifact, owner and synthetic-data boundary.', 'steps': ['**Stage 1 — Preflight and validate assumptions/environment.** Create `day-155-02-build-the-operating-evidence-row-for.md`. Record Day 155, the prior artifact, the source `https://services.google.com/fh/files/misc/v6.1_pca_altostrat_media_case_study_english.pdf`, the access date, a named owner and the statement that the exercise uses synthetic or tabletop evidence only.', '**Stage 2 — Prepare the target, inputs, or backing resources.** Inventory. List artifact, model, prompt, index, data, reviewer and deployment versions.', '**Stage 3 — Author the plan, configuration, or analysis.** Map signals. For each version identify one success metric, one failure signal, one owner and one rollback action.', '**Stage 4 — Execute or simulate the planned change.** Inject drift. Change one model setting or run one worker with an older configuration. Record the first detectable mismatch.', '**Stage 5 — Inspect expected state and verify outcomes.** Cost-check. Add the main storage, inference, transfer, retry and human-review cost drivers; flag any current pricing lookup.', '**Stage 6 — Rehearse a bounded failure, edge case, or decision challenge.** Review. Ask whether an incident responder can tell what changed and stop unsafe publication.', '**Stage 7 — Diagnose evidence and record remediation/decision.** Save. Append the operating matrix to the ADR and link it from the exit artifact.', '**Stage 8 — Clean up or close out the exercise.** Save `day-155-02-build-the-operating-evidence-row-for.md`, link it from the daily artifact, keep the evidence, remove only disposable copies and state what needs an authorized or production verification.'], 'verification': 'A traceable operating matrix that makes AI quality, cost, release and hybrid drift observable.', 'accept': 'The saved artifact identifies the requirement, selected and rejected options, acceptance evidence, failure response, owner and residual risk.', 'trouble': 'If a metric has no decision owner or response, it is a dashboard decoration; assign the owner or remove the claim.', 'cleanup': 'Keep the evidence artifact and remove only disposable copies. No cloud resource, credential, payment detail or protected exam content belongs in this exercise.', 'file': 'day-155-02-build-the-operating-evidence-row-for.md'}}]}
